WEBVTT

00:03:57.059 --> 00:04:00.301
It's the speech he gives
to all the people in Montgomery

00:04:00.325 --> 00:04:03.249
four days after Rosa Parks
has been arrested.

00:04:03.273 --> 00:04:04.911
At the end of the speech, he says,

00:04:04.935 --> 00:04:08.293
one day, they're going to tell a story

00:04:08.317 --> 00:04:10.546
about a group of people

00:04:10.570 --> 00:04:12.026
in Montgomery, Alabama.

00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:15.118
And then he says, of Black people
who stood up for their rights,

00:04:15.142 --> 00:04:18.254
and when they stood up for their rights,
the whole world changed.

00:04:18.278 --> 00:04:22.150
And you had an immediate response
to that call to action.

00:04:22.174 --> 00:04:24.403
JL: That message really appealed to me.

00:04:24.427 --> 00:04:25.586
BS: Yeah.

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:29.139
JL: It was sort of
a social gospel message.

00:04:29.163 --> 00:04:30.314
BS: Yeah.